<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto"><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/Chrome_incompatibilities" rel="nofollow">The Chrome Incompatibilities page for WebExtensions APIs</a> is missing Chrome's <code class="notranslate">debugger</code> API in its "Unsupported APIs" section. This will inform extension developers that the API is only available in Chrome.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">I discovered that this API was missing Firefox support when developing an extension myself, so I want others to be informed.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/api/debugger" rel="nofollow">Chrome's debugger API documentation</a></li>
<li><a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1316741" rel="nofollow">Firefox's intention not to implement the API</a></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto">None that I know of.</p>



]]></content>
